{"version":2,"slug":"how-to-learn-the-8-parts-of-speech","videoId":"YsB27xBV2CU","videoUrl":"https://youtu.be/YsB27xBV2CU","lang":"en","title":"How to Learn the 8 Parts of Speech","category":"Travelling","channel":"English by Jay - Sprout","channelUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/@englishbyjay.official","captionSource":"auto","tags":["Slow english","simple english learn"],"backUrl":"/","lines":[{"start":0,"text":"Every name is called a noun, as carrot"},{"start":2,"text":"and book, sky,"},{"start":5,"text":"and ground."},{"start":7,"text":"In place of noun, the pronoun stands, as"},{"start":10,"text":"he and she can clap their hands. An"},{"start":13,"text":"adjective describes a thing, like"},{"start":15,"text":"colorful pens or diamond ring. The verb"},{"start":19,"text":"[music] means action, something done, to"},{"start":22,"text":"read,"},{"start":23,"text":"to sip,"},{"start":25,"text":"to lift weights,"},{"start":26,"text":"to run."},{"start":30,"text":"How things are done, the adverbs tell,"},{"start":33,"text":"as quickly,"},{"start":34,"text":"slowly,"},{"start":36,"text":"badly,"},{"start":37,"text":"or well."},{"start":39,"text":"A preposition"},{"start":41,"text":"shows relation, as"},{"start":44,"text":"in the armchair,"},{"start":46,"text":"or at the station."},{"start":50,"text":"Conjunctions"},{"start":51,"text":"[music]"},{"start":51.6,"text":"connect many words, like cats and dogs,"},{"start":56,"text":"bees or birds."},{"start":58,"text":"The interjection cries out, \"Ah! We need"},{"start":62,"text":"an exclamation mark.\" Through poetry,"},{"start":65,"text":"we learn how each of these make up"},{"start":68,"text":"the parts of speech."},{"start":73,"text":"Just like these Jenga blocks, the"},{"start":76,"text":"English language has eight core parts of"},{"start":80,"text":"speech, and they form the structure"},{"start":82,"text":"behind everything from casual"},{"start":85,"text":"conversation to Shakespeare's plays."},{"start":89,"text":"[cheering]"},{"start":89.6,"text":"Let's break down each one and see how"},{"start":92,"text":"they build"},{"start":94,"text":"a sentence."},{"start":98,"text":"A noun names a person,"},{"start":100,"text":"a place,"},{"start":102,"text":"a thing,"},{"start":103,"text":"or an idea."},{"start":105,"text":"A person, like Jay,"},{"start":108,"text":"Mario,"},{"start":110,"text":"Peach."},{"start":111,"text":"A thing, like a phone."},{"start":114,"text":"The phone has a screen."},{"start":117,"text":"I can tap the screen. These are apps."},{"start":123,"text":"And look."},{"start":125,"text":"Sprout, we have"},{"start":127,"text":"an app. Sprout, you can download that"},{"start":130,"text":"now in the App Store and Google Play to"},{"start":133,"text":"immerse yourself in English. Download"},{"start":136,"text":"now."},{"start":138,"text":"[music]"},{"start":139,"text":"If nouns are the actors,"},{"start":143,"text":"verbs"},{"start":144,"text":"are the actions."},{"start":146,"text":"For example, the dog runs."},{"start":149,"text":"Run is the verb. It shows us the action"},{"start":153,"text":"taking place."},{"start":154,"text":"But verbs don't always show movements."},{"start":158,"text":"Some verbs describe states of being."},{"start":161,"text":"She is happy."},{"start":164,"text":"They seem tired. I [snorts] know"},{"start":168,"text":"the answer."},{"start":170,"text":"[music]"},{"start":172,"text":"Now, let's add"},{"start":175,"text":"some color. Adjectives turn a plain,"},{"start":178,"text":"boring sentence into something"},{"start":180,"text":"[snorts]"},{"start":180.6,"text":"more colorful. Instead of just saying"},{"start":182,"text":"the dog runs, we can say a small, brown"},{"start":187,"text":"dog runs. This is a soft,"},{"start":191,"text":"comfy,"},{"start":192,"text":"yellow"},{"start":194,"text":"cushion."},{"start":198,"text":"Adverbs describe verbs,"},{"start":201,"text":"adjectives, or even other adverbs. And"},{"start":205,"text":"most often, they describe"},{"start":207,"text":"how something happens."},{"start":209,"text":"For example,"},{"start":210,"text":"the dog runs quickly."},{"start":214,"text":"The dog runs slowly."},{"start":217,"text":"Or, the dog runs excitedly because it's"},{"start":221,"text":"seen a red frisbee."},{"start":223,"text":"Many adverbs end in L Y,"},{"start":227,"text":"but not all."},{"start":229,"text":"Some adverbs describe when"},{"start":232,"text":"or how much."},{"start":233,"text":"For example, I am reading"},{"start":236,"text":"now."},{"start":238,"text":"Now is the adverb."},{"start":240,"text":"The water is very cold."},{"start":243,"text":"Adverbs add precision"},{"start":247,"text":"to actions."},{"start":253,"text":"Can you guess the mistake here? Jay goes"},{"start":256,"text":"to the park."},{"start":258,"text":"Jay feeds bread to the geese."},{"start":261,"text":"Jay puts on his pink bike helmet, and"},{"start":264,"text":"Jay rides a horse into the blue sky."},{"start":269,"text":"Instead of repeating Jay, to make the"},{"start":272,"text":"sentence sound smoother, we would say"},{"start":275,"text":"Jay goes to the park. He feeds bread to"},{"start":278,"text":"the geese."},{"start":280,"text":"He rides off on his horse into the blue,"},{"start":283,"text":"blue sky. Common pronouns include I,"},{"start":286,"text":"you, he, she, it, we,"},{"start":290,"text":"and they."},{"start":291,"text":"And these pronouns help your sentences"},{"start":294,"text":"sound less"},{"start":296,"text":"clunky"},{"start":297,"text":"and more smooth."},{"start":302,"text":"Prepositions show the relationship"},{"start":305,"text":"between words,"},{"start":307,"text":"often involving location"},{"start":311,"text":"or time."},{"start":312,"text":"For example, imagine me and a lion. I"},{"start":315,"text":"could be in front of the lion,"},{"start":318,"text":"under the lion,"},{"start":322,"text":"behind the lion,"},{"start":323,"text":"or if I'm feeling adventurous,"},{"start":326,"text":"on the lion."},{"start":329,"text":"Without prepositions, sentences would"},{"start":332,"text":"lose"},{"start":335,"text":"their sense of space."},{"start":340,"text":"Just like a plant connects to the soil,"},{"start":344,"text":"a conjunction connects words,"},{"start":347,"text":"phrases,"},{"start":348,"text":"or sentences."},{"start":350,"text":"For example,"},{"start":351,"text":"I like coffee"},{"start":353,"text":"and tea."},{"start":355,"text":"Or, I was tired, but I kept working."},{"start":360,"text":"Common conjunctions include and"},{"start":363,"text":"but"},{"start":364,"text":"or"},{"start":365,"text":"because and so."},{"start":367,"text":"They allow ideas to grow and sentences"},{"start":370,"text":"to flow."},{"start":375,"text":"Interjections express"},{"start":378,"text":"sudden emotion"},{"start":381,"text":"or reaction."},{"start":382,"text":"For example,"},{"start":383,"text":"wow."},{"start":390,"text":"Ouch."},{"start":391,"text":"Oh, no."},{"start":394,"text":"Interjections come at the beginning of a"},{"start":396,"text":"sentence and they usually have an"},{"start":399,"text":"exclamation mark."},{"start":401,"text":"They bring a bit of personality and"},{"start":404,"text":"feeling into the language."},{"start":407,"text":"So, remember this simple guide. Nouns"},{"start":410,"text":"name things."},{"start":411,"text":"Verbs show action."},{"start":414,"text":"Adjectives describe [music]"},{"start":415,"text":"nouns."},{"start":417,"text":"Adverbs describe verbs."},{"start":420,"text":"Pronouns"},{"start":421,"text":"[music]"},{"start":421.6,"text":"replace nouns."},{"start":423,"text":"Prepositions show position."},{"start":426,"text":"Conjunctions connect ideas"},{"start":429,"text":"and interjections show emotion. If you"},{"start":434,"text":"enjoyed this video and you want to speak"},{"start":437,"text":"with JI, which is an AI version of me,"},{"start":440,"text":"then you can go to sproutlanguage.com or"},{"start":443,"text":"you can download the app. Yes, we have"},{"start":445,"text":"an app now. Download it. Link in"},{"start":447,"text":"description. You can speak more about"},{"start":448,"text":"this and practice your English further."},{"start":450,"text":"[music]"},{"start":450.6,"text":"I hope it helps. I hope you still keep"},{"start":452,"text":"learning and stay positive, people."},{"start":455,"text":"Thank you. Much love."}]}